NAME
    wmps - process viewer WM client (Path C phase 23)

SYNOPSIS
    wmps [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Open a 420x320 window listing the running processes (pid,
    state, name) — the same data as the CLI `ps` reads from
    /proc/<pid>/status.  Refreshes automatically every 1 second.

    Keyboard (focus required):
      Up / Down arrow   move selection
      r / R             refresh immediately
      q / Q / Esc       quit

    Clicking a row selects it.  Selection is visual only — no
    actions yet (a future session could add 'k' to send SIGKILL
    via sys_kill once we wire SYS_KILL through the focused
    keystroke stream).

    Three columns: PID (left), STATE (middle), NAME (right).
    Column widths are hand-padded — the libgfx 8x8 font is
    monospace so the columns line up.

SEE ALSO
    wmd(1), wmsysinfo(1), wmfiles(1), ps(1)
